Z||000011||dogtired||11-18-1999||01:55 PM||||GREAT STORY<BR>Reminds me of me back in High School mid 60's. I had a 57 chev 6cyl (235.5 CI) I always made sure to emphasise the .5, like it made a big difference.  Automatic (power slip) Car wouldn't get out of its own way. Anyway a friend had a Falcon 6cyl 3speed. Except for the cappuccino you pretty much described our race.<BR>Would I tell you this story if I lost?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000012||RFMike||11-18-1999||07:07 PM||||Olympic, you just made my day.  Had a tough day, but fell off my chair laughing when I read your exploits.<BR>Dogtired, my first car was a 57 Chevy with a 265 v8 from a 56 nomad.  The old man and I rebuilt it and put it in.  Had a 4 barrel and dual exhaust, 2-speed auto.  It wasn't fast, but it was fun.  I not only beat a Ford Falcon, I waxed a Plymouth Valiant, among other noble contestants.  I loved that car.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Patrick||11-18-1999||07:18 PM||||<BR>You know, you guys are really going to make it difficult for <B>olympic</B> to know what to say in response. I may be wrong, but I don't believe these are his exploits. The heading of this thread is "<B>a funny story I found</B>".<P>Nevertheless, great story <B>olympic</B>. Thanks for passing it on. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000014||olympic||11-18-1999||08:01 PM||||You're right Patrick, this is a story I downloaded, and just like everyone else who read it I fell to the floor laughing(I still can't read it with a straight face!!) If it will make you all happy, tonight I'll borrow my girlfriends Suzuki with 1.6L(emphasis on the POINT SIX) of raw power on 13 inch rims and try to live out the story  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>One problem though, the town where I live is so small that there are no 4 lane streets(or Yugos for that matter) to race on. Hey,wait a minute, maybe if I hurry downtown I can catch the old ladies coming out of bingo and race one of them on their motorized scooters. Yeeeaaaah, I can feel the adrenaline flowing just thinking about it. Blue hair or not she's goin' down tonight.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||10
